In article <349e7e0b.1554362825@news.cwru.edu>,
Jon Fiedler <jmf9@po.cwru.edu> wrote:
>I've got an AXPpci33 motherboard with (supposedly) 32 MB ram
>installed.  However, the system only recognizes 24 MB.  Is there some
>flag that you can set the memory size?  Are there any issues with
>memory on this motherboard?

It's definitely time to incorporate this issue into some periodic post or
something -- it seems like every AXPpci33 user hits this snag!

The problem is that MILO doesn't bother autosizing the memory on an AXPpci33,
and assumes you have 24 MB unless you tell it otherwise.  To do that, type
"setenv MEMORY_SIZE 32"
at the MILO> prompt and everything should be great.

John Wilson
