Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha


Hello;

Background:
Alpha PC164
128 MB RAM
SCSI card - ncr53c810 chipset
SCSI driver - ncr53c810 NOT the 53c7,8xx driver
harddrives - 2 ST32550N's 1 Quantum Fireball ST3.2S
Linux - RedHat 4.2

/dev/sda -- ST32550N harddrive -- Linux drive
/dev/sdb -- ST32550N harddrive -- NT4.0
/dev/sdc -- ST3.2S   harddrive -- Linux drive

The /dev/sda harddrive developed several bad blocks which required
the drive to be reformatted. Before restoring the filesystems from tape
the ran the following:
badblocks -b 1024 /dev/sda3 1536000

consistantly I receive a scsidisk error message in /var/log/messages concerning
sector 2163128.

I decided to run badblocks in read/write mode with the following command:
badblocks -b 1024 -s -v -w /dev/sda3 1536000

This command fails and basically hangs the machine for awhile til it can be 'killed'.
I receive the following message:
"Couldn't get a free page..." which is coming from /usr/src/linux/mm/kmalloc.c

Before I dive into this problem has anyone else ever seen this problem?

I am able to run the read/write test by doing it in 100000 block segments.
i.e.
badblocks -b 1024 -s -v -w /dev/sda3 100000 000000
badblocks -b 1024 -s -v -w /dev/sda3 200000 100000
badblocks -b 1024 -s -v -w /dev/sda3 300000 200000
...
badblocks -b 1024 -s -v -w /dev/sda3 1536000 1500000

I do not receive the same errors as the read-only test.
I receive several different sectors as being unrecovered read errors, the sectors
are all in the same cylinders however.

I will need to reformat the drive once again, but why does badblocks in read/write mode
interact so negatively with kmalloc? I have never seen this message before running
