Terry L. Ridder wrote:

> consistantly I receive a scsidisk error message in /var/log/messages concerning
> sector 2163128.
>

As the error occurs always at the same block this seems a hard disk failure. Even if this
is not so frequent nowadays it is not unusual. Both 'fsck' and 'mkfs' have the possibility
to scan the disk looking for bad blocks and registering the damaged sectors in a bad block
list. Run either:

    mke2fs -c [your_flags] /dev/sda3

or
    e2fsck -c /dev/sda3

As you have an empty partition the first one seems the best. It will take longer but you
will get your disk up and running.

Good luck!!

--
Carlos Vidal
