Yes.  I just bought a 500 Mhz Screamer, and it is very fast.  I can't
compare it to the Pentium II/300 Mhz because we don't have one handy.
I have compared it to our IBM RS/6K and SGI Indy-2 and it is well
worth the money!

> Is Linux stable on them,?

Yes.  Mine came preinstalled with Redhat 4.2 and it works great.
Actually Microway set mine up as a tri-boot (DEC-Unix, RedHat Linux,
Microsoft-NT) so I can experiment and get some of my DEC-Unix apps
over to the Linux side.  Everything works great.

