X-windows working on the Linux boot yet (couldn't find a video card
that would work with all of the OSs).  Microway has committed to
provide this (a lower-end card) if a Linux driver doesn't become
available soon.  Right now, the machine spends most of the time
crunching numbers under DEC-Unix (but could just as well be under
Linux) and I don't need a GUI on the console anyway.

