Hannu Karhu <hankarhu@utu.fi> writes:

> What is the current state of the g77 compiler on the Alpha?
> How fast is it?

g77 built on the egcs-1.0 distribution seems fairly stable (runs
SPECfp correctly, although f2c libs do have bugs in namelist),
and is maybe 30% or so slower than Digital Fortran. g77 built
on the gcc-2.7.2.3 backend can be much, much slower on code
with arrays with 2 or more dimensions. I don't think we're
keeping a webpage yet of SPECfp comparisons but I will
do that once I get my first PC164LX system.

-- g



