Hi

You need the milo for an avanti and also the kernel for an avanti.
I guess you have put linload.exe and milo in a boot option. Otherwise you
would not get this pal code message.
In stead the option 'nodebug' you can put in :

boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
But you have to swap the milo disk fast for the bootdisk when you do this
because in starts immediately loading when milo has restarted the comp.

later you can change that in

boot sda#:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda# with # the number of the partition.

I use the arc console myself and it works ok. So you don't need the srm
I use the following setup

run cd:\alpha\arcinst.exe and make a 10mb dos partition.

start linux from flop: redhat 5.0 or whatever:

run fdisk delete the extending partition if arcinst made one.
make a linux partition sda2 and a swap sda3 (128mb will do)
leave some space for windows nt if you want that also.

I have now on a 2gb disk

10mb dos partition
1200mb linux root
128mb swap
670mb nt partition.

copy linload.exe and milo to the 10mb dos partition
I use \os\linux\linload.exe
and \os\linux\milo
And made a boot option entry for it. So you don't need floppies anymore.

for the 670mb partition I had to run arcinst.exe again to format the nt
partition. 

Anyway I have now 2 boot options linux and nt. with linux the default one.


have fun with your alpha

Paul 

