Hey Mark,

The included kernel headers/sources from the RedHat4.2 won't work.
I suggest to get 2.0.32 instead of 2.0.30, works like a dream on my
Alpha.

Get the 2.0.32 Linux kernel from:
ftp://ftp.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v2.0/linux-2.0.32.tar.gz

Get the alpha kernelpatches from:
ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/alpha-patches-2.0.32-0.1.gz

        cd /someplace-not-usr-src
        tar xzvf /archive/linux-2.0.32.tar.gz
        cd linux
        zcat /archive/alpha-patches-2.0.32-0.1.gz | patch -p1 -E >&
../log
        make config
        make dep
        make boot

Optionally you can do "make modules; make modules_install" too.

Have fun with your new 2.0.32 kernel;-)

Regards,
Antoine



