Edwin Klemann wrote:

> I used the following boot line.
> MILO> boot sda5:/os/linux/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

The line is OK, but this is for use _after_ the linux install,
you better do it the 3 floppy disk way, this works for sure...

1. The Milo disk (the Milo XL or Avanti.img)
2. The Kernel disk (XL or Avanti.img)
3. The Ramdisk disk 

Make an entry in the ARC loader for the bootfloppy:

LOADIDENTIFIER=Linux Install Floppy
SYSTEMPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
OSLOADER=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)\linload.exe
OSLOADPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
OSLOADFILENAME=\milo
OSLOADOPTIONS=

This will boot Milo from disk1, when you get the Milo prompt,
FIRST insert disk2 (the kernel, xl.img) then type:

MILO> boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

After loading the kernel you'll be asked to place the 3rd disk (ramdisk)
and if all went well, the RedHat install screen should appear...

> Has anybody any expirience with Rh5 and an XL266 and can anybody tell me
> what the difference is between the avanti kernel and the xlt kernel ???

XL	= XL233 & XL266 (sometimes also called Avanti).
XLT	= XL300 & XL366 (sometimes also called Ancor?).

I haven't tried RH-5.0 yet (i'm still downloading it) but if you follow
my directions, this should work;-)

Good luck,
Antoine



