On 8 Dec 1997 13:32:00 GMT, Richard B. Kreckel <kreckel@iphcip1.physik.uni-mainz.de> wrote:
>ones. What is the philosophy behind this aggressive update-behaviour?
>(Is there anybody actually testing the suff at RedHat?)

As some fundamental data types changed between glibc 1.99 and glibc 2.x on
the Alpha, the only safe way of supporting apps compiled against both is
to have a shared libs compiled against both. We didn't feel like there
were enough binary-only alpha programs floating around to justify having
to keep up with two sets of shared libraries.

