glenn@bluedream.com wrote:
> 
> Does Linux/Alpha support PCMCIA modems?
> 
 
yes:

Compile module support into the kernel (grab latest stable or
experimental kernel sources - avoid the ones that come with the Red Hat
distribution) - ignore Red Hat's documentation that says modules are not
possible on Alpha (that was only true a _long_ time ago).

Download the latest version of the pc-card module (2.9.?) and Module
Utils (5.5) - compile and install.  On boot up cardmgr should find and
detect its UART - it will first probe it as a memory card when checking
the two slots - don't worry. 

I've had it working on my 2.0.30 kernel, RH4.1 UDB box with two
different modems (Megahertz XJ144 and a generic 33.6 one) for the past 4
months.  Having Linux/Alpha's inherent binary compatibilty is the next
best thing to having OSF1/Digital Unix at home.

