: Is there anybody how can explain to me what i need to get it running ?

: The board is a Digital AXPpci 33 with a 21066 Alpha chip on 166Mhz.
: This is all i have. What do i have to buy (power source, memory, vga,
: etc....)?
You'll need at least:

2 x 72 pins real parity (36 bits) fast page SIMMS. 
  (SIMMCITY, http://www.simmcitysite.com/, has these)

1 SCSI cdrom. 1 SCSI cable. 1 harddisk (SCSI recommended)
1 (S)VGA card.

Standard AT Case, with a standard AT power supply 
 (there are two power connector on the mainboard. You have to
  connect the AT power plugs with the second one:

       +-this one is for the AT power plug
       |      +-- this one is not needed
       V      V   don't use it !
 --------------------+
       |:     |:     | 
       |:     |:     |

2 Serial ports (cable+connector), 1 Parallel port(cable+connector).

There are versions of the AXPpci33 that use a PS/2 keyboard, as well
as versions of the AXPpci33 that use a standard AT keyboard. You'll
have to check what version you have.

: Any information is welcome. I would like to run it with WindowsNT 4.0
: Workstation

Do you have the OEM Design Guide? A postscript version is downloadable
from ftp.digital.com, /pub/DEC/axppci/design_guide.ps. Please read it.

Regards, Onno Hovers (now a happy alpha user)



